### Task 4 — Validity Audit

| Threat | Description | Control / Disclosure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Hardware Heterogeneity** | Differences in memory bandwidth between CPU (DDR) and GPU (VRAM) skew results. | Disclose exact RAM/VRAM speeds and bus widths used. |
| **Implementation Divergence** | The Vulkan backend might use different kernels or precision than the CUDA backend. | Use the exact same model weights and quantization parameters across all backends. |
| **Resource Contention** | The 8-thread CPU limit may cause thermal throttling or context switching not present in GPU runs. | Monitor and report clock speeds and thermal states during all three runs. |
| **Workload Comparability** | The CPU run might use a different "prompt processing" algorithm (e.g., different batch size) than the GPU. | **Control:** Ensure the prompt length, temperature, and sampling parameters are identical; force the same batch size for prompt evaluation. |

